      "title": "From application to agreement",
      "narration": "Marcus signs an application and pays an initial premium. Has he automatically received every benefit he requested? Not necessarily. A valid contract needs agreement, consideration, competent parties and a legal purpose. The application commonly constitutes an offer, and the insurer decides whether to accept under its rules. If it offers different coverage or a higher premium, that may be a counteroffer requiring acceptance. The precise effective date also depends on the application, receipt and policy conditions. A signature or payment alone is not a universal coverage rule.",
